# Portable Software Engineering Harness — Cursor Adapter

For meaningful implementation, remediation, migration, review, release, or pre-PR work, load `/harness-run`.

Authoritative source:

```text
.harness/core/
.harness/agents/
.agents/skills/
```

`.cursor/` contains execution adapters only.

Invariants:

- Classify work mode, scope, and risk before selecting gates.
- `change size != change risk`.
- Run the smallest complete specialist set.
- Never skip a materially REQUIRED gate.
- Use `.cursor/agents/` for routed specialist work.
- Review specialists are read-only.
- All agents in one review wave inspect the same stable change identity.
- Independent specialist reviews may run in parallel.
- New material findings create dynamic routing triggers.
- Reviewer does not run until all REQUIRED gates are terminal.
- A specialist blocker cannot be averaged away.
- Missing required evidence is not PASS.
- After remediation, rerun only materially invalidated gates.
- Only `PRE_PR_PASS` or `PRE_PR_PASS_WITH_CONDITIONS` permits PR transition.
- Any material post-gate edit makes final readiness stale.
